  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Textual description mapped onto visual subjects",
  "description": "The text 'kids enjoying some underwater diving' is overlaid on the image of two young Black girls in shallow water. The text falsely maps the visual subjects (the girls) onto the concept of 'underwater diving,' which is not what they are doing. This creates an analogical mapping where the girls are implicitly equated with 'underwater divers' — a term that, in context, reinforces racialized stereotypes about Black people's swimming abilities. The mapping is direct: the text labels the visual entities as engaging in a specific activity (underwater diving) that they are not actually performing.",
